Spec: Project/Map

Purpose:
  Routing/index only — answers "where do I go?", nothing more. Detailed
  knowledge (flow, DB, API, cases) lives inside each module's own folder,
  never here (per prompt/new/9.md correction: a global file must not grow
  into "the entire system's map in one file").

Project: EduNexus

ProjectMap:

Modules:
  payment -> ./project/payment
  course  -> ./project/course
  user    -> ./project/user

Domains:
  # NOTE: the source (prompt/new/11.md) repeats the same module list under
  # both "Modules:" and "Domains:" here — this is module-level "Domains"
  # (business domain = same thing as Modules in this router's context), NOT
  # the discipline-level "Domains:" (Backend/Frontend/Mobile/QA/DevOps)
  # used in PROJECT.sdd. Kept as the source states it rather than silently
  # merged, to avoid inventing a resolution the chat itself hasn't made yet.
  payment -> ./project/payment
  course  -> ./project/course
  user    -> ./project/user

Paths:
  BE -> ./backend
  FE -> ./frontend
  MD -> ./mobile
  QA -> ./qa
  DO -> ./devops
  # NOTE (prompt/new/14.md): these are lookup references for where AI
  # should find real project code once it exists — NOT an instruction to
  # scaffold these folders now. .sdd/ is built by hand (this repo); the
  # real project (backend/, frontend/, ...) is built later by a separate
  # prompt engine, driven by this model. Do not create these folders here.

Rules:
  A module MUST have its own project model.
  Module knowledge MUST stay inside its module directory.
  Global map MUST contain routing information only.
  Do not duplicate module details here.

Resolve:
  payment -> ./project/payment/payment.sdd
  course  -> ./project/course/course.sdd
  user    -> ./project/user/user.sdd

Flow:
  feature -> module/flow.sdd

Navigation:
  USER INPUT
    -> PROJECT.sdd
    -> map.sdd
    -> IDENTIFY MODULE
    -> Resolve[module]  (module/*.sdd)
    -> IDENTIFY REQUIRED FLOW -> module/flow.sdd
    -> CURRENT STAGE -> LOAD STAGE SKILLS
    -> LOAD ONLY WHAT'S NEEDED: db.sdd? api.sdd? cases.sdd?
    -> WORK -> VALIDATE -> UPDATE STATE -> NEXT FLOW NODE

Status:
  payment/, course/, user/ module folders and their payment.sdd/flow.sdd/
  db.sdd/api.sdd/cases.sdd already exist (built ahead, in prompt/new/9.md's
  step) — course/ and user/ are still stubs. This is further along than
  prompt/new/11.md's own pacing ("STEP 2 is map.sdd only, don't create the
  module folders yet"), which is fine: this repo applies accumulated
  knowledge as it's read, not a strict re-enactment of the original chat's
  step-by-step reveal order.
